I've got a chaotic elven priestess (randomly chosen by the RNG) which
was reasonably lucky early in the game - was able to pick up a BoH
lying around on the floor (!!) within the first 3 dungeon levels, and
was also able to randomly find a +oID, which she blessed and learned.
Also bought a blessed magic lamp from Izchak (already blessed, mind
you) and got Mjollnir.  Another shop also had a magic marker for sale.

The mines happened to yield a ring of conflict - so I got a pretty
powerful ring relatively early in the game (the earliest I ever got
this before was around DL12 in the main dungeon, and only from a
polypile, not randomly generated)

Unfortunately Sokoban provided a BoH also, so I just took the gold and
went to buy protection (since I was wearing a lousy studded leather
armor to improve my spellcasting).

I then got the luckstone from the mine's end, or rather, a pet of mine
did, which then stepped on a level teleport trap.  I didn't notice it
happening, of course, so after finding a cursed gray stone that failed
the kick-test and scouring the entirety of the mine's end, I went up,
found the pet again, and soon found the luckstone.

With luckstone in hand I went down to explore some levels in the main
dungeon, periodically returning to my DL2 converted altar and to the
minetown priest to donate.  Found a wand of polymorph and polypiled
some stuff, getting some nice ?oEA and ?oEW, then upgraded my shirt to
+4 and the robe to +3.

I then crept down to DL13, and got the telepathic message from the
High Priest.  I ignored this since I was only XL12 and went back down
to DL14.

While passing through a corridor, some random troll zapped a wand.
The ray just misses.  The ray was black.  What was particularly nasty
was that I was approximately right in the middle of a straight
corridor, meaning I had no way of avoiding a straight-line zapping of
the /oD.  With neither reflection nor magic resistance, I had no
chance against /oD.

Fortunately, I happened to have a /oTele in my open inventory, so I
zapped the troll with it, ran to the upstairs (which was fortunately
near, and was not where the troll got teleported to) and decided to
bum around until I could get to XL13, after which I could drink the
blessed !oGL I had been reserving to get into the quest for.

Soon I was qualified for the quest and went down to the quest level.
After getting somewhat mobbed at the temple of Nalzok, I took out a
scroll of taming and tamed the undead around.

Since one of the traps in the temple was a polymorph trap, I decided
to try pushing some of the pet undead into it, hoping to get a
reasonably faster and/or more powerful pet.  Unfortunately, a mistype
pushed me onto the trap instead, polymorphing me (and I had been
hoping to keep polyselfless conduct!) and breaking my shirt, armor,
and robe.  With the robe gone, I began losing levels (MC 0, right?).
Fortunately, I soon located the hostile priest of Moloch (he'd
teleported himself away from me) and relieved him of his robe and
armor, getting back the needed MC.

I soon made my way down to the level above Nalzok's lair.  A randomly
picked up ?oMap that was being an encumberance showed me that the
downstair was in a crowded graveyard, but while making my way there a
trapdoor opened up, putting me near Nalzok's lair.

After hitting him a few times, he summoned nasties.  I engraved an
Elbereth on the upstair, only to realize that one of the nasties was a
minotaur who quickly reduced my life to about half.  I ran up the
stairs, right into the crowded yard, and took out my last ?oTame,
taming about a third of the undead there.  After recuperating for a
while, I went back down to try to solve the problem of the minotaur,
but Nalzok wrecked my nice +3 helmet (a pet had shoplifted it for me).
so I went back up.  Unfortunately Nalzok followed me, but with the pet
undead around me I was reasonably safe from him.

Soon, however, I got tired of hanging around the pet undead (and was
running out of food, too) so I read a scroll of tele, found myself in
the room next to the upstair, and started bashing Nalzok after he
teleported away from the upstair.  He summoned nasties again, and I
engraved Elbereth, and *then* noticed that he had summoned a minotaur
*again*, who this time got my life to about a third.  Grr.

So I rushed out of the quest branch to think things over.

Without the (old and wrecked) +4 shirt and the (old and wrecked) +3
robe and the (old and wrecked) +3 helmet my AC is only -5 or
thereabouts; it had been around -15 or so before the accident and the
problem of Nalzok wrecking my armor.  I can't go down safely to the
castle, not without MR, because of the troll with the /oD.  I haven't
ID'ed genocide yet, so I can't do the desperation move of reverse
genociding silver/gray dragons for their scale.  I have only one
polymorph wand charge remaining, and have not yet ID'ed charging -
otherwise I would have tried polypiling a bunch of scrolls on the
chance that one would become genocide.  My MM is about 0:50ish.

I have completed my ring kit: conflict, levitation, free action, and
slow digestion.  Only tele control is missing.

My weapon is the +2 Mjollnir, and my armor is the robe (now +2), a
leather armor from the hostile priest of Moloch, and water walking
boots.  No helm because it got wrecked by Nalzok.

So now, I'm kind of stuck.  My armor sucks because Nalzok kept
wrecking them, and I don't have MR or reflection to counter the troll
with the /oD.  Nalzok keeps summoning non-Elbereth-respecting
monsters.  Any suggestions?



